; The rules read the shipped workflow files, so those files are deps of the
; runtest action: editing one reruns the check against it. The globs name every
; workflow and every composite action, in both spellings GitHub accepts, so a
; file added later is copied into the build tree and checked without editing
; this list. The Dockerfile is read for the same reason: its base images are
; checked as they ship.

(test
 (name test_workflow_rules)
 (modules test_workflow_rules workflow_rules)
 (deps
  (glob_files %{project_root}/.github/workflows/*.{yaml,yml})
  (glob_files_rec %{project_root}/.github/actions/action.{yaml,yml})
  %{project_root}/Dockerfile)
 (libraries alcotest test_helpers yaml))
